OrionLayer open fix 120 — the end-of-game score screen on the wire
===================================================================

Work order 403 (package B). orion2re on the fork's branch `orionlayer`
(v2.0.0), on top of open fix 119 and its README row. Not on
`orionlayer-local`. In src/ext/ext_api.cpp, src/ext/ext_api.h and
src/game/score.cpp, under ORION2RE_EXT.

When a game ends (nextturn.cpp:49-83) the engine runs
SCORE::End_Of_Game_Hi_Score (score.cpp:138-200), whose first step is
Hi_Score_Screen (score.cpp:490-545): Draw_Hi_Score_Screen (:86-120) prints
nine components from SCORE::hi, which Calculate_Hi_Scores (:816-845) fills.
The Hall of Fame follows (open fix 50). The screen ran under its caller's
id and the nine numbers were on no block.

The change. Hi_Score_Screen reports the synthetic id 87 (SCREEN_EXT_SCORE,
the next free one after 86 in both trees) through a ScreenOverride and sets
ext::g_score_live just before its loop; the flag is cleared when the loop
ends. While both hold, SerializeState writes "SCOR" before FILM: uint8
version (1), int16 the player the tally is for (hi->player_idx), int16 the
whole-screen hidden field that ends it (hi->screen_field_handle, hotkey ESC,
score.cpp:985-987), the nine scores in the order time, population,
elimination, captured colonists, technology, Orion, Antares, council, then
the raw subtotal, the modifier in percent and the final score (int16 each),
the raw numbers the lines print (stardate figure of the time line, raw
population, opponents defeated, captured colonies), the lines as the game
formats them (uint8 length and bytes, at most 80: time, population,
elimination, captured colonies, technology, Orion, Antares, council (empty
when its score is not above 0), the total's label and its figure), the
player's name and race name (20), then uint8 n defeated players and per
player uint8 index, uint8 race, int16 the defeat's figure (printed "%d.%d"
by tenths) and the name. The strings use the same H_Message ids and
formats as the Draw_* functions (score.cpp:638-812, :847-); the pictures
of population icons (Draw_Pop) are not sent. Read only.

Live: UNVERIFIED — no live run (work order 403 does not run the engine).
Built on the scratch clone `~/claude/clones/403_orion2re` (`linux-debug`,
ORION2RE_EXT on); score.cpp and mainscr2.cpp also compiled without
ORION2RE_EXT; a misspelt call (`g_score_liveX`) is refused by the compiler.

